# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Byte-exact policy: do NOT translate line endings.
#
# This repository publishes SHA-256 values for the delivery artifacts
# (`deliverables_semi/复赛结果_棒材优化.zip` / `.json`) and for the code archive,
# and `deliverables_semi/复赛代码与模型.zip` is claimed to be byte-reproducible.
# With the machine default `core.autocrlf=true` and no attributes, git rewrites
# CRLF<->LF on commit/checkout, which has two consequences a reviewer can hit:
#
#   * the byte count of a file in the repository differs from the byte count of
#     the same file inside the code archive (e.g. `validation_report.json` was
#     11,084 B in the repo and 11,407 B in the archive);
#   * `make_code_zip.py` would rebuild a DIFFERENT archive hash on Linux, where
#     checkout yields LF instead of CRLF.
#
# Declaring the tree as non-text (`-text`) stops git from converting anything:
# what is committed is exactly what `make_code_zip.py` reads and hashes, on any
# platform.  Diffs stay readable -- git still treats these files as text for
# diff purposes; only the EOL filter is disabled.
#
# The shell scripts' executable bit is irrelevant here (Windows-hosted repo).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* -text
